      "lineNbr": 365,
      "author": {
        "id": 1862735
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-09T09:30:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "node_id filtering is used to find out the real culprit. We couldn\u0027t rely solely on pid as current transaction is not necessarily the method call that is responsible for overflowing the transaction buffer, it may be the normal async transaction but happens to reach the detection threshold. In the new design, I\u0027ll return back 5 BR_SPAM_SUSPECT if the 5 different nodes related buffers all seems like spamming (number \u003e 50 or alloc size \u003e 256K). But if the node related buffers not like spamming, then no need to dump their backtrace.",
      "parentUuid": "ba941b2f_417f574a",
      "revId": "e0a4de19033328cd0443721bb94c06d0af159397",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
